  "description": "FUZBEI crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H69 Ce6 N6 O38 1-,H4 N1 1+,3(C3 H7 N1 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce1B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.728-3.844 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.05-119.62°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula NH4[Ce6(μ3-O)5(μ3-OH)3(μ2-C6H5COO)9(NO3)3(DMF)3]·DMF·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(V).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
